Windows CI: rustkit-renderer scroll_cost_tests::culling_never_changes_coverage_or_order_of_decorations_negative_sizes_or_wide_borders
compares a culled frame with the unculled one pixel for pixel (text within 1 LSB on glyph pixels). On the
hosted runner's software adapter (WARP) it fails since refresh #21 brought hiwave-macos #1348: the
per-character glyph path now resolves `sans-serif` to Arial, as Chrome on Windows does (before, it fell
back to Segoe UI), and WARP rasterises the two frames differently (locally 1 pixel, 1 LSB, outside glyph
pixels; on the runner 4 glyph pixels, one by 14). It passes on a hardware GPU (RTX 4090), and passed on
WARP at refresh #21's batch-110 head. It skips on a software adapter, as 649 skips a GPU timing.

Remove when the comparison holds on WARP, or the runner gets a GPU.

